{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785586329,"nonce":"cybH0yySQC+8wB1pVXITUoPQ9pQ=","message":"**Done at `56220d7`.** All four boxes:\n- [x] st_dev at startup (`durability_tier`: S3→object; LocalDir compared by device against warm — a second PVC counts, same device does not); verdict threaded into `WorkspaceState.tier` and served on `GET /v1/tier`.\n- [x] Warm-only supported + loud: warn+println at boot with the exact consequence (\"Succeeded is licensed by the warm volume alone\"); flush/settle answer `200 durable:false tier:warm-only` — never a 503 loop, because nothing about warm-only is repaired by retry. Same-device cold is NOT written (waste + false comfort). The GC residue detector suppresses under a warm-only answer, stays ON on a probe error (a torn cold must not be maskable by breaking /v1/tier), and `scarab_cas_gc_tier_probe_failed` tells the two apart.\n- [x] `attempts.output_durability` (migration 0042), stamped via a REQUIRED `Executor::output_durability` riding the same crash-atomic Pod-annotation patch as root+identity. NULL = pre-s2 / no workspace / old-Depot skew — the stamp never guesses.\n- [x] On the wire: `AttemptDto.output_durability` (+ `failure_detail`, stored since 0041 but never served). UI copy is the remaining cosmetic follow-up.\n\nThe \"required, not defaulted\" ruling immediately caught SecretInjectingExecutor AND CloneEnrichingExecutor swallowing `output_identity` via the defaulted method — skip-if-unchanged could never fire on secrets-wired deployments. Fixed + tested through the production nesting.\n\n**Honest hole, disclosed in ADR-0064's amended table:** st_dev proves independence from warm, not persistence — a cold LocalDir on its OWN emptyDir passes and still dies with the Pod. That check belongs to the Helm chart; follow-up noted in the ADR.","files":null}]}